---Definition for a shortcut button in the [shortcut bar](https://wiki.factorio.com/Shortcut_bar).
---
---This is **not** a custom keybinding (keyboard shortcut), for that see [CustomInputPrototype](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/CustomInputPrototype.html).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html)
---@class (exact) ShortcutPrototype:Prototype
---@
---
---If this is `"lua"`, [on\_lua\_shortcut](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/events.html#on_lua_shortcut) is raised when the shortcut is clicked.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23action#action)
---@field action ("toggle-alt-mode")|("undo")|("redo")|("paste")|("import-string")|("toggle-personal-roboport")|("toggle-personal-logistic-requests")|("toggle-equipment-movement-bonus")|("spawn-item")|("lua")
---@
---
---Name of a custom input or vanilla control. This is **only** used to show the keybind in the tooltip of the shortcut.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23associated_control_input#associated_control_input)
---@field associated_control_input? string
---@
---
---Path to the icon file.
---
---Only loaded, and mandatory if `icons` is not defined.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23icon#icon)
---@field icon? FileName
---@
---
---The size of the square icon, in pixels. E.g. `32` for a 32px by 32px icon. Must be larger than `0`.
---
---The base game uses 32px icons for shortcuts.
---
---Only loaded if `icons` is not defined.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23icon_size#icon_size)
---@field icon_size? SpriteSizeType
---@
---
---Can't be an empty array.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23icons#icons)
---@field icons? (IconData)[]
---@
---
---The item to create when clicking on a shortcut with the action set to `"spawn-item"`. The item must have the [spawnable](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemPrototypeFlags.html%23spawnable#spawnable) flag set.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23item_to_spawn#item_to_spawn)
---@field item_to_spawn? ItemID
---@
---
---Used to order the shortcuts in the [quick panel](https://wiki.factorio.com/Quick_panel), which replaces the shortcut bar when using a controller (game pad). It [is recommended](https://forums.factorio.com/106661) to order modded shortcuts after the vanilla shortcuts.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23order#order)
---@field order? Order
---@
---
---Path to the icon file. Used in the shortcut selection popup.
---
---Only loaded, and mandatory if `small_icons` is not defined.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23small_icon#small_icon)
---@field small_icon? FileName
---@
---
---The size of the small icon, in pixels. E.g. `32` for a 32px by 32px icon. Must be larger than `0`.
---
---The base game uses 24px small icons for shortcuts.
---
---Only loaded if `small_icons` is not defined.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23small_icon_size#small_icon_size)
---@field small_icon_size? SpriteSizeType
---@
---
---Can't be an empty array.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23small_icons#small_icons)
---@field small_icons? (IconData)[]
---@
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23style#style)
---@field style? ("default")|("blue")|("red")|("green")
---@
---
---The technology that must be researched before this shortcut can be used. Once a shortcut is unlocked in one save file, it is unlocked for all future save files.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23technology_to_unlock#technology_to_unlock)
---@field technology_to_unlock? TechnologyID
---@
---
---Must be enabled for the Factorio API to be able to set the toggled state on the shortcut button, see [LuaPlayer::set\_shortcut\_toggled](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaPlayer.html#set_shortcut_toggled).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23toggleable#toggleable)
---@field toggleable? boolean
---@
---
---If `true`, the shortcut will not be available until its `technology_to_unlock` is researched, even if it was already researched in a different game.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ShortcutPrototype.html%23unavailable_until_unlocked#unavailable_until_unlocked)
---@field unavailable_until_unlocked? boolean
---@
